---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHead from "../../components/PageHead.astro";
import AppShot from "../../components/AppShot.astro";

const rows = [
  ["Where the secrets live", "Encrypted backups on Twilio's servers, tied to your phone number", "An encrypted file on your Mac"],
  ["Account", "Required", "None"],
  ["Source", "Closed", "Open source, Apache-2.0"],
  ["Desktop", "The desktop apps were discontinued in August 2024", "A native macOS app and the tess CLI"],
  ["Phone", "iOS and Android", "None yet"],
  ["Export", "No export", "tess export, the app's vault export, and otpauth links or QR codes per account"],
  ["Price", "Free", "Free"],
];
---
<Base
  title="Tessera vs Authy"
  description="Authy keeps your codes on Twilio's servers behind your phone number; Tessera keeps them in a file on your Mac. What differs and how to move."
  current="/vs/authy"
>
  <PageHead kicker="Compared" title="Tessera vs Authy.">
    Authy is a hosted authenticator from Twilio. Tessera is a local one. The difference is where the secrets live and who can get at them.
    <AppShot slot="media" sizes="(min-width: 900px) 34vw, 80vw" />
  </PageHead>

  <div class="measure cmp">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th></th><th>Authy</th><th>Tessera</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {rows.map(([k, a, b]) => (
          <tr><th scope="row">{k}</th><td>{a}</td><td>{b}</td></tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 class="h-sub mt-14">Pick Authy if</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 soft list">
      <li>You want codes on a phone with a backup you never think about, and do not need a desktop app.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h-sub mt-12">Pick Tessera if</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 soft list">
      <li>You work on a Mac and want the code where the login happens, in a window or in a shell.</li>
      <li>You want to read the vault format and the code that implements it.</li>
      <li>You do not want a phone number or an account between you and your codes.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h-sub mt-12">Moving from Authy</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 soft">
      Authy has no export, so each account is re-enrolled: on the service's security page, turn two-factor off and on again, then scan the new QR with Tessera (on screen, from the app) or save it and run <span class="mono">tess add code.png</span>. Keep Authy installed until the last account has moved.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 soft">Facts about Authy were checked on 2026-08-22 and may have changed.</p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .cmp { padding-block: 1rem 6rem; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  th, td { text-align: left; vertical-align: top; padding: 0.8rem 1rem 0.8rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  thead th { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.05rem; }
  tbody th { color: var(--ink); white-space: nowrap; }
  td { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .list li { padding-left: 1.1rem; position: relative; }
  .list li + li { margin-top: 0.5rem; }
  .list li::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.72em; width: 0.4rem; height: 0.4rem; border-radius: 2px; background: var(--gold); }
</style>
